--
With the Ackermann pairs of `a with [i := v]` left out, an index that is a
different expression but the same value as i must still read v: the with
constraints now say so (j == i => x[j] == v) for every other index of the
set. Here the store goes through an SSA symbol, whose own pairs still cover
it, so this passes either way today; it pins the behaviour for when symbols
lose their pairs too.
